description:
Docs/code claim: docs/SEMANTIC_DONOR_SPEC.md:95-98 requires SEM-ITR-001: iterator closing (`return`) runs on abrupt completion in for...of; docs/SEMANTIC_DONOR_SPEC.md:133-134 requires break, throw, and return paths to trigger iterator close. iterator_protocol.rs:230-236 models IteratorClose with a return_called flag.

Reality gap: the executed runtime close path ignores user iterator return methods. lowering_pipeline.rs:1895-2000 emits IteratorClose only for the explicit break label, and baseline_interpreter.rs:6381-6397 implements close_iterator by marking the internal RuntimeIteratorState closed/done. It never looks up or calls iterator.return(), and the reason argument is unused. The current behavior can only close FrankenEngine-internal Vec-backed iterator state.

Concrete reproducer:
```js
let closed = 0;
const iterable = {
  [Symbol.iterator]: function() {
    return {
      next: function() { return { value: 1, done: false }; },
      return: function() { closed = 1; return { done: true }; }
    };
  }
};
for (const value of iterable) { break; }
closed; // expected 1 under IteratorClose; current close_iterator cannot call return().
```

Also cover throw/return from loop body, not only break. This is a fail-closed semantic gap: evidence can record an IteratorClose event with return_called=true, but the production runtime has no path that performs that call.

