ENHANCEMENT (PearlTower audit): Adding adapter trait signatures, error types, schema versioning, and migration contract.

## Adapter Trait Signatures
```rust
trait StorageAdapter: Send + Sync {
    // Evidence persistence
    fn store_evidence(&self, entry: &EvidenceEntry) -> Result<EngineObjectId, StorageError>;
    fn load_evidence(&self, id: &EngineObjectId) -> Result<Option<EvidenceEntry>, StorageError>;
    fn query_evidence(&self, filter: &EvidenceFilter) -> Result<Vec<EvidenceEntry>, StorageError>;

    // Replay index
    fn store_replay_index(&self, entry: &ReplayIndexEntry) -> Result<(), StorageError>;
    fn load_replay_range(&self, trace_id: &TraceId, range: TimeRange) -> Result<Vec<ReplayIndexEntry>, StorageError>;

    // Benchmark ledger
    fn store_benchmark_result(&self, result: &BenchmarkResult) -> Result<EngineObjectId, StorageError>;
    fn load_benchmark_result(&self, id: &EngineObjectId) -> Result<Option<BenchmarkResult>, StorageError>;
    fn query_benchmark_trend(&self, suite_id: &str, limit: usize) -> Result<Vec<BenchmarkResult>, StorageError>;

    // Policy artifact cache
    fn store_policy_artifact(&self, artifact: &PolicyArtifact) -> Result<(), StorageError>;
    fn load_policy_artifact(&self, id: &EngineObjectId) -> Result<Option<PolicyArtifact>, StorageError>;

    // Schema management
    fn current_schema_version(&self) -> Result<u32, StorageError>;
    fn migrate_to(&self, target_version: u32) -> Result<MigrationReceipt, StorageError>;
}
```

## Error Types
```rust
enum StorageError {
    NotFound { id: EngineObjectId },
    SchemaVersionMismatch { expected: u32, actual: u32 },
    MigrationFailed { from: u32, to: u32, reason: String },
    IntegrityViolation { table: String, detail: String },
    ConnectionFailed { detail: String },
    QueryFailed { query: String, detail: String },
    SerializationFailed { type_name: String, detail: String },
    ReadOnly { operation: String },
}
```

## Schema Versioning Strategy
- Schema version stored in a metadata table (schema_version INTEGER PRIMARY KEY)
- Migrations are forward-only: each version N has a migrate_N_to_N+1() function
- Migration functions are deterministic: given the same database state, produce identical results
- Migration produces a MigrationReceipt { from: u32, to: u32, tables_modified: Vec<String>, rows_affected: u64, hash_before: ContentHash, hash_after: ContentHash }
- Incompatible schema versions fail with explicit SchemaVersionMismatch error (never silent upgrade)

## SQLite Configuration (via frankensqlite)
- WAL mode enabled for concurrent reads
- PRAGMA journal_size_limit = 67108864 (64MB)
- PRAGMA busy_timeout = 5000
- Connection pool with max 4 writers, 16 readers
- All writes wrapped in transactions for atomicity

