Docs/code claim: docs/SEMANTIC_DONOR_SPEC.md:58-67 makes arrays-and-iteration a high-impact mandatory semantic domain, and crates/franken-engine/src/iterator_protocol.rs:3-8 says the module implements ES2020 iterator protocol support for for..of/spread/destructuring.

Reality gap: baseline for..of does not perform GetIterator / @@iterator lookup. crates/franken-engine/src/baseline_interpreter.rs:6305-6317 calls collect_for_of_values, and crates/franken-engine/src/baseline_interpreter.rs:17509-17538 only accepts strings or object numeric properties sorted as array-like values. It never calls a user-defined Symbol.iterator method or iterator.next(). Meanwhile crates/franken-engine/src/lowering_gap_inventory.rs:202-210 records this as resolved and says for-of executes as a real iterator-protocol loop.

Concrete reproducer:
```js
const iterable = {
  [Symbol.iterator]: function() {
    let i = 0;
    return {
      next: function() {
        return i < 3 ? { value: i++, done: false } : { done: true };
      }
    };
  }
};
let out = "";
for (const value of iterable) { out = out + value; }
out; // expected "012"; current runtime treats the object as non-iterable unless it has numeric array-like keys.
```

Impact: ES2015+ compatibility and any proof artifact claiming real iterator protocol execution are overstated. Fix should route for..of/spread/destructuring through GetIterator, captured next method, IteratorResult validation, and fail-closed TypeError paths for invalid iterables.

